---
/**
 * Cross-section of a sealed insulated glass unit (IGU), drawn to answer the
 * one question the fogged-windows guide exists to settle: is the haze
 * between the panes (a failed seal, no fix but replacement) or on the room
 * side of the glass (condensation, a humidity problem)? A photo of foggy
 * glass cannot show *where* the moisture sits. A section through the glass
 * can.
 *
 * Same token-driven palette as the other diagrams — currentColor and the
 * design system's CSS custom properties, no hardcoded hexes.
 */
interface Props {
  heading?: string | null;
}
const { heading = 'Where the moisture actually is' } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="glass-detail">
  {heading && <figcaption class="glass-heading">{heading}</figcaption>}

  <div class="glass-pair">
    <div class="glass-panel">
      <p class="glass-title">Failed seal</p>
      <p class="glass-sub">Fog is between the panes</p>

      <svg
        class="glass-svg"
        viewBox="0 0 240 180"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Cross-section of an insulated glass unit with a failed seal: the spacer has let go, argon gas has escaped, and moisture and haze sit between the two panes of glass where a cloth cannot reach."
      >
        <rect x="10" y="10" width="220" height="160" class="g-frame" rx="4" />

        <rect x="70" y="24" width="14" height="132" class="g-pane" />
        <rect x="156" y="24" width="14" height="132" class="g-pane" />
        <rect x="84" y="24" width="6" height="132" class="g-coat" />

        <rect x="90" y="26" width="66" height="12" class="g-spacer-broken" />
        <rect x="90" y="142" width="66" height="12" class="g-spacer-broken" />

        <g class="g-fog">
          <circle cx="105" cy="60" r="7" />
          <circle cx="122" cy="78" r="9" />
          <circle cx="140" cy="58" r="6" />
          <circle cx="112" cy="100" r="8" />
          <circle cx="135" cy="115" r="7" />
          <circle cx="150" cy="95" r="6" />
        </g>

        <line x1="120" y1="12" x2="120" y2="24" class="g-lead" />
        <line x1="120" y1="156" x2="120" y2="168" class="g-lead" />
        <text x="120" y="172" class="g-label">Sealed between panes — cannot wipe off</text>
      </svg>

      <ul class="glass-notes">
        <li><span class="swatch s-broken"></span>Spacer seal has let go</li>
        <li><span class="swatch s-fog"></span>Insulating gas is gone; haze stays</li>
        <li>Only fix is a new glass unit or window</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel">
      <p class="glass-title">Room-side condensation</p>
      <p class="glass-sub">Moisture is on the inside face</p>

      <svg
        class="glass-svg"
        viewBox="0 0 240 180"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Cross-section of a sound insulated glass unit: the seal is intact, gas fill remains between the panes, and condensation instead beads on the room-side face of the interior pane where warm humid air meets cold glass."
      >
        <rect x="10" y="10" width="220" height="160" class="g-frame" rx="4" />

        <rect x="70" y="24" width="14" height="132" class="g-pane" />
        <rect x="156" y="24" width="14" height="132" class="g-pane" />
        <rect x="84" y="24" width="6" height="132" class="g-coat" />

        <rect x="90" y="26" width="66" height="12" class="g-spacer-ok" />
        <rect x="90" y="142" width="66" height="12" class="g-spacer-ok" />

        <text x="123" y="90" class="g-fill-label">Argon</text>

        <g class="g-drip">
          <circle cx="182" cy="52" r="2.6" />
          <circle cx="192" cy="68" r="3" />
          <circle cx="184" cy="86" r="2.4" />
          <circle cx="196" cy="104" r="2.8" />
          <circle cx="186" cy="122" r="2.2" />
          <circle cx="194" cy="138" r="2.6" />
        </g>

        <path d="M176 20 L176 158" class="g-room-line" />
        <text x="176" y="12" class="g-label" text-anchor="middle">Room side</text>

        <line x1="120" y1="12" x2="120" y2="24" class="g-lead" />
        <line x1="120" y1="156" x2="120" y2="168" class="g-lead" />
        <text x="120" y="172" class="g-label">Seal intact — can be wiped off</text>
      </svg>

      <ul class="glass-notes">
        <li><span class="swatch s-ok"></span>Seal and gas fill are still good</li>
        <li><span class="swatch s-drip"></span>Warm indoor air meets cold glass</li>
        <li>A humidity and ventilation problem, not the window</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="glass-foot">
    Look at the haze from an angle. If it sits inside the two panes where a cloth cannot reach,
    the seal has failed. If it wipes off the inside face, it is condensation — a fan and a
    tighter, warmer window both help, but the glass itself is not the problem.
  </p>
</figure>

<style>
  .glass-detail {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .glass-heading {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-m);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-display);
  }

  .glass-pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  .glass-panel {
    padding: var(--space-m);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .glass-title {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3xs);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }

  .glass-sub {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .glass-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--paper-sunk);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .g-frame {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }

  .g-pane {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 10%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--ink-soft);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .g-coat {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
  }

  .g-spacer-ok {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 20%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }

  .g-spacer-broken {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 18%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--danger);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
  }

  .g-fog circle {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 30%, transparent);
  }

  .g-drip circle {
    fill: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .g-room-line {
    stroke: var(--ink-faint);
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-dasharray: 2 3;
  }

  .g-fill-label {
    fill: var(--ink-faint);
    font-family: Outfit, 'Outfit Fallback', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 8px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-anchor: middle;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    writing-mode: vertical-rl;
  }

  .g-label {
    fill: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: Outfit, 'Outfit Fallback', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 8.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .g-lead {
    stroke: var(--ink-faint);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .glass-notes {
    margin: var(--space-s) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3xs);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .glass-notes li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .swatch {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    flex: none;
    translate: 0 0.1rem;
  }

  .s-broken {
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--danger);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 18%, transparent);
  }

  .s-fog {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 30%, transparent);
  }

  .s-ok {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 20%, transparent);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .s-drip {
    background: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .glass-foot {
    margin: var(--space-m) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .glass-pair {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
